-- title:
--   Moduli reading of a supersingular point of the cyclotomic two-chart model
-- statement:
--   The data fixed in the hypotheses fall into five groups.
--
--   *Arithmetic data.* A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$.
--
--   *Cyclotomic base field and function field.* A field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $\{q\ell\}$, an element $\zeta \in L$ that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, an element $\xi \in L$ that is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with `hK` asserting that $K$ is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q * ℓ) ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q * ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH (q * ℓ) M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times$, the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$.
--
--   *Base discrete valuation ring.* A domain $A$ which is a discrete valuation ring, an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, the hypothesis `hAq` that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$, the hypothesis `hζA` that $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$, and a uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$, i.e. `hϖ` states that the maximal ideal of $A$ is generated by $\varpi$.
--
--   *The $j$-line datum and the two-chart model.* An element $j \in K$ whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ is the coefficientwise image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function, with $j \ne 0$. Here [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebras of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, respectively over $A[j^{-1}]$. A point $z$ of this scheme is given, together with the element $\varpi z$ of the stalk at $z$ defined by `hϖz` as the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ through the structure morphism [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258) to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and `hz` requires $\varpi z$ to lie in the maximal ideal of that stalk, so that $z$ lies over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$. A point $y$ of the finite chart `XFin A K j` $= \operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` is given with `hy` asserting that the chart immersion `ιFin` sends $y$ to $z$.
--
--   *Supersingularity at $y$.* The hypothesis `hss` states that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite-chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime $y$, the value $\varphi(\,$`jChartFin`$\,) = \varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-trivial $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of the following package.
--
--   A ring $A_0$, a domain and a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and whose residue field is finite; an $A_0$-algebra structure on $A$ with injective structure map making $A$ a finite $A_0$-module; an element $\zeta_A \in A$ mapping to $\zeta$ in $L$ and with $A_0[\zeta_A] = A$; units $\ell$ and $M'$ in $A_0$.
--
--   Two stability hypotheses over $A_0$: `hℓ`, that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData` $D$, a level-$\ell$ structure on $W$ (the six conditions of `IsLevelPStructure`: both points satisfy the affine equation, both abscissae are roots of `preΨ ℓ`, and the two `indepElt` expressions are units) transports to one on $C \bullet W$ with $D$ replaced by `D.variableChange C`; and `hM`, that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (i.e. `IsTwoKernel h` when $p^k = 2$, and `IsCyclicGenKernel p k h` otherwise) transports to `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k` of the transformed kernel polynomial `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`.
--
--   Group-law data over $A_0$: a family of relative group laws $\mathcal{G}$ on the projective Weierstrass models of curves with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras, which is chord–tangent (`IsChordTangent`) and has the origin as identity (`IsOriginIdentity`), together with a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`, i.e. its variable-change and coefficient-change actions on raw Drinfeld pairs are compatible with the induced maps of projective models on the two marked sections. Two further hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and projective Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, graded ring homomorphisms on `projModelGradingCR` realising a variable change $C$, respectively a coefficient homomorphism $f$, in the sense of `IsVariableChangeHom` and `IsCoefficientHom`, each subject to the stated inequality between irrelevant ideals.
--
--   A fine moduli package $P_0$ of type `LevelModuliPackageAbs A₀ (rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯).toLevelModuliDatum` — so $P_0$ consists of an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ and a universal point `P₀.univ` over $B_0$ of the moduli datum obtained from the product of the $\Gamma_0$-power component at $M'$, the level-$\ell$ component and the level-$q$ Drinfeld component, such that every point over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of `univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $B_0 \to T$ — and $B_0$ is of finite type over $A_0$.
--
--   A maximal ideal $\mathfrak{p}$ of $B_0$ containing the image of $q$, supersingular in the same sense as above: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : B_0 \to \Omega$ with kernel $\mathfrak{p}$, $\varphi(P_0.j_0) \in$ [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), where $P_0.j_0 \in B_0$ is the $j$-invariant attached to the universal point.
--
--   A ring isomorphism $\beta$ from the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ at its maximal ideal onto the $\mathfrak{p}$-adic completion of $B_0$; a ring homomorphism $\sigma_0 : A \to \widehat{B_{0,\mathfrak{p}}}$ which on $A_0$ agrees with $A_0 \to B_0 \to \widehat{B_{0,\mathfrak{p}}}$; and the two hypotheses `hjK`, that the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q * ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the level-$q\ell$ expansion of the $q$-expansion of $j$) lies in $K$, and `hjC`, that this element of $K$ lies in the finite-chart algebra.
--
--   Writing $STK$ for the stalk at $z$, $CMP$ for its adic completion, $toC$ for the canonical map $STK \to CMP$, and $germY$ for the ring homomorphism from the finite-chart algebra to $STK$ obtained from the germ at $z$ on the open image of `ιFin` composed with the inverse of the `appIso` of `ιFin` at $\top$ and the inverse of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ isomorphism of the chart algebra, the package satisfies three conjuncts.
--
--   First, compatibility with constants: for every $a \in A$, applying $\beta$ to the image in $CMP$ of the germ at $z$ of the global section determined by $a$ through `toBase` gives $\sigma_0(a)$.
--
--   Second, $\beta\bigl(toC\,(germY\,\langle\,$`jqNModC L (q * ℓ)`$\,\rangle)\bigr)$ equals the image of $P_0.j_0$ in $\widehat{B_{0,\mathfrak{p}}}$.
--
--   Third, there are a ring homomorphism $\theta_K : B_0 \to K$ and a proof `hθK` that $\theta_K b$ lies in the finite-chart algebra for all $b$, such that: every element of the finite-chart algebra is of the form $\theta_K b$ for some $b \in B_0$; for every $b \in B_0$ one has $\beta(toC(germY\,\theta_K b)) =$ the image of $b$ in $\widehat{B_{0,\mathfrak{p}}}$; and the following dictionary for level automorphisms holds. For every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in $\Gamma_0(M')$, every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q * ℓ) ξ (q * ℓ) ((q * ℓ) ^ 2 * M') (levelH (q * ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — the condition that, for all weights and all pairs of modular forms for the relevant $\Gamma_H$ with integral $q$-expansions, $\tau$ acts on ratios of $q$-expansions as the slash action by the matrix `conjElemN (q * ℓ) γ⁻¹`, read through any embedding of $L$ into $\mathbb{C}$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$ — and every proof `hpres` that $\tau$ maps the finite-chart algebra into itself, if the restriction of $\tau$ to the chart algebra is congruent to the identity modulo the prime $y$ (that is, $\tau(a) - a \in y$ for every $a$ in the chart algebra), then there exists an automorphism $\rho_\gamma$ of the moduli problem, i.e. an element of `ProblemAut` of `(rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯).toLevelModuliDatum` (a natural self-map of the points functor preserving the $j$-invariant), with four properties:
--
--   (i) on points over fields: for every field $T$ which is an $A_0$-algebra and all raw points $x, x'$ of `rigidDataPow` over $T$ with the discriminant of the Drinfeld component's curve of $x$ a unit, if $x'$ has the same curve as $x$, the same $\Gamma_0$-power component, level-$\ell$ component equal to the relabelling `LevelRelabelling.LevelPData.relabel` of that of $x$ by the integral matrix $\gamma$, and Drinfeld component equal to `LevelRelabelling.RawDrinfeldPair.relabel 𝒢` of that of $x$ by $\gamma$, then $\rho_\gamma$ sends the class of $x$ to the class of $x'$;
--
--   (ii) $\theta_K \circ P_0.\mathrm{classify}(\rho_\gamma\cdot P_0.\mathrm{univ}) = \tau \circ \theta_K$ on $B_0$, where $P_0.\mathrm{classify}(\rho_\gamma \cdot P_0.\mathrm{univ})$ is the endomorphism of $B_0$ classifying the image of the universal point under $\rho_\gamma$;
--
--   (iii) that endomorphism is congruent to the identity modulo $\mathfrak{p}$: $P_0.\mathrm{classify}(\rho_\gamma \cdot P_0.\mathrm{univ})(b) - b \in \mathfrak{p}$ for all $b \in B_0$;
--
--   (iv) if $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$, then $\gamma \notin \Gamma(\ell)$.
--
--   This is the moduli-theoretic reading of a supersingular point of the cyclotomic two-chart integral model of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$: it identifies the completed local ring at such a point with a completed local ring of the representing algebra of the corresponding rigidified level structure problem, matching constants, the $j$-invariant at the Tate parameter and, through the surjection $\theta_K$ onto the chart algebra, the action of level automorphisms attached to elements of $\Gamma_0(M')$ with automorphisms of the moduli problem given by relabelling. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_regularLocalRing_isDrinfeldBasisAdic_const_hasseParam_levelAut_linearPart_of_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_regularLocalRing_isDrinfeldBasisAdic_const_hasseParam_levelAut_linearPart_of_mem_ssJSet), where the adic picture is refined to a Drinfeld-basis description of the completed local ring together with the linear part of the level automorphisms.
